# Security headers for Cloudflare Pages
# See: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# The main Content-Security-Policy (script-src / style-src with SHA-256 hashes,
# img/font/connect/frame sources) is generated per page by Astro
# (`security.csp` in astro.config.ts, sources in src/config/csp.config.ts) and
# emitted as a <meta http-equiv="content-security-policy"> tag.
#
# The header below only carries directives a <meta> tag cannot set
# (frame-ancestors) plus a few hardening defaults. Browsers enforce both
# policies, so the header must not add script-src/style-src restrictions.
#
# HSTS: one year, without includeSubDomains/preload so a fork's custom domain
# can't accidentally lock subdomains to HTTPS. Add them once you're sure.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# Fingerprinted build assets never change.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
